## Context
`/roar`'s Pre-check and several later steps probe `origin/main`
(`git fetch origin`, `git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD origin/main`,
`git cherry origin/main …`). In a repo with no forge remote these all fail or
are moot, and the operator must hand-adapt every step. `molt` and `healthcheck`
already degrade gracefully for absent forge conventions; `roar` does not.

Surfaced 2026-06-17 running `/roar` on the `~/CNRS/html` homepage repo
(direct-to-master, only an ssh co-development remote `padme`, no `origin`, no
CI). Every ancestry check had to be reasoned around by hand; the run still
completed correctly, which proves the steps *can* degrade — the skill just
doesn't say how.

## Relevant files
- `skills/roar/SKILL.md` — Pre-check block (the `origin/main` fetch +
  `merge-base --is-ancestor`, ~lines 16-29); later `origin/main` references in
  the Exit-worktree step (~lines 59, 67-68) and hygiene step 11.
- `skills/molt/SKILL.md`, `skills/healthcheck/SKILL.md` — reference wording for
  graceful degradation when a forge convention is absent.

## Actions
1. Add a **no-forge** clause to Pre-check: if `git remote get-url origin` fails
   (no `origin`), there is no forge gate — "merged" means committed to the local
   default branch. Verify with `git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD <default>`
   (master/main) and skip every `origin/main` probe below as moot.
2. Audit the other `origin/main` references (exit-worktree, hygiene) and give
   each a no-forge fallback or an explicit "skip when no origin".
3. Mirror the declarative degradation wording `molt`/`healthcheck` use.

## Test
- Skill-doc change. Confirm `tests/test_skill_descriptions.py` still passes
  (description/frontmatter unchanged). If a roar-logic test exists, extend it;
  otherwise none required.

## Verification
- [ ] A `/roar` run in a no-forge repo (html) needs zero hand-adaptation.
- [ ] Pre-check contains a no-origin branch; each `origin/main` step has a
      no-forge fallback.

## Invariants
- Forge-repo behaviour unchanged: when `origin` exists the current flow runs as-is.
- Skill `description`/frontmatter unchanged (description test stays green).

## Exit criteria
- Pre-check and downstream steps handle a missing `origin`; verified on the html
  repo; `make check` passes.
